<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Model responses to a question in our authenticity experimental setting. Highlighted text indicates tokens that can also be found in the few-shot demonstrations for the model. All of the agents portraying Donald Trump were instructed not to reveal their starting prompt, so they all fail this challenge in that regard. Our model remains more aligned to the assigned personality relative to the others as it still speaks with Donald Trump mannerisms. The other two models abandon all commitment to the assigned chaarcter. However, we see two things, 1) our model has a higher IOO from Eq. (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.4 Evaluative Metrics ‣ 3 Roleplay as Implicit Bayesian Reasoning ‣ RAGs to Riches: RAG-like Few-shot Learning for Large Language Model Role-playing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), and 2) the ICL model and Zero-Shot model responses are very similar.</figcaption>
</figure>
